# Semantic execution integrity

This Livebook is both documentation and an executable specification. The cell
marked `ash_r2rml_test` is executed by the normal ExUnit suite and CI. The
notebook demonstrates the DfCM contract without granting filesystem, database,
or cutover authority.

```elixir ash_r2rml_test
import ExUnit.Assertions

xsd_string = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"

profile = %{
  ontology_hash: "ontology:livebook",
  profile_hash: "profile:livebook",
  shacl_hash: "shacl:livebook",
  resources: [
    %{
      iri: "https://example.org/resource/Person",
      class_iri: "https://schema.org/Person",
      shape_iri: "https://example.org/shapes/PersonShape",
      module: "Livebook.Person",
      repo_module: "Livebook.Repo",
      table: "people",
      subject_template: "https://example.org/people/{id}",
      identities: [%{name: :primary, keys: [:id], primary?: true}],
      attributes: [
        %{
          name: :id,
          column: "id",
          predicate_iri: "https://example.org/ontology/id",
          datatype_iri: xsd_string,
          ash_type: :uuid,
          postgres_type: "UUID",
          min_count: 1,
          max_count: 1,
          nullable: false,
          identity?: true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{:ok, first} = AshR2RML.DfCM.Compiler.compile(profile)
{:ok, replay} = AshR2RML.DfCM.Compiler.compile(profile)

assert first.session_identity.sha256 == replay.session_identity.sha256
assert AshR2RML.DfCM.Compiler.receipt_reusable?(first, replay)
assert first.integrity_receipt.standing == :projections_deterministic
refute AshR2RML.DfCM.Compiler.cutover_ready?(first)

plan =
  AshR2RML.Manufacturing.plan(
    %{"generated/example.txt" => "stable"},
    first.session_identity
  )

assert {:ok, verification} = AshR2RML.Manufacturing.verify_staged(plan, plan.file_hashes)
assert verification.verified?
assert AshR2RML.SemanticValue.kind(AshR2RML.SemanticValue.null()) == :null
assert AshR2RML.SemanticValue.kind(AshR2RML.SemanticValue.unbound()) == :unbound

:all_green
```

A passing notebook establishes only the construction contracts it actually
executes. It does not establish PostgreSQL, external OBDA, subject parity, or
cutover standing; those require their own observed receipts.